    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Verifies that plain text (i.e., text without the {@code ${...}} prefix/suffix notation) is left unchanged, while variables that ARE wrapped in {@code ${...}} are resolved. <p>In the template {@code \"The animal jumps over the ${target}.\"}, the word {@code animal} appears as literal text — it has no surrounding {@code ${}} markers — so it is NOT substituted. Only {@code ${target}} is resolved (to {@code \"lazy dog\"} from the values map), producing {@code \"The animal jumps over the lazy dog.\"}.</p>"
